      "value": "@{6216b5c74124f104e4bcd3ad|full_name} That's a really good point.  I've also met plenty of trusted users who were toxic or straight up criminal.  But I think a large part of the problem is the fact that any group can host public group worlds.  \n\n2 years ago I actually had a problem with a single dude who was running all the instances of the Great Pug using 3-4 different groups on like 6+ accounts.  He banned me from them because I was part of a 'Gender Fluid' group after I called him out for laughing at a guy for having autism in his bio (and kicked that guy too).  So for a few months I was basically locked out of the Great pug because of this one guy hosting all the instances using his various groups and alts.  It was absolutely bullcrap.\n\nSo I don't know what a better solution would be.  But I think it's too easy to set up a group, host a group public, and use some friends or alts to populate it a bit to get it going.  And then harassing or abusing people in the worlds with no repercussions.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
