  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I am suggesting improving the group block feature to hide the groups from the world lists and give you a confirmation if you attempt to join a world a group you have blocked is hosting.  \n\nIn addition to this, I think you should implement a trust system for groups similar to how you have for users.  Before Group Public worlds became the norm, you could just block toxic players in publics and still have a decent time.  Players who were blocked a lot would have their rank decreease.\n\nNow me and most of my friends are finding those same toxic players we used to block are the ones hosting the group public worlds which is leading to the worst public experiences we've ever had in the game in 8 years as these toxic players now in positions of power use it to bully and harass people with no consequences.   Every lobby you join now is a dice roll if some power hungry moderator is going to kick you because you're too quiet, or because they don't like your avatar, or because you refuse to give them personal information, or because you're LGBT or a minority, or because you spoke to the girl/guy they like, or because you muted a moderator spamming music over the mic, or because they're just having a bad day.  \n\n My group of friends have countless stories of how we got kicked for the dumbest reasons and we actively avoid group public worlds now because we don't know who is running them and we're exhausted of the negative experiences.  We can't simply block toxic players anymore because we risk getting kicked.\n\nThe common suggestion from the community when you complain about this problem is to research and memorize which groups are good and which ones are bad.  This is extremely time consuming and mentally draining and you can only do it by having constant negative experiences.   I think VRChat needs a better way to either remove groups being run by toxic players, or give the community the power to rank/derank these groups based on interactions.  Perhaps if a group gets blocked enough they lose the privilege of hosting group public worlds.\n\nIf the Group Block system is improved, perhaps this can be used for determining which groups are actually decent communities, and which are just power hungry toxic individuals getting their kicks being in a position of power.",
